    "summary": "This 1968 Imperial Crown two-door hardtop was delivered new to Perkins Motor Company of Colorado Springs, Colorado, and it is said to have been kept by its second owner and their family from 1969 through 2021. The car was repainted in a shade of bronze in 2022, and the interior is trimmed in brown leather and patterned gold-colored cloth. Powered by a 440ci V8 paired with a three-speed automatic transmission, the car is equipped with a Sure-Grip rear end, a dual exhaust system, turbine-style wheel covers, whitewall tires, power steering, front disc brakes, rear fender skirts, a brown vinyl roof, automatic climate control, an AM/FM stereo, an eight-track player, power windows, a power-adjustable front bench seat, and tilt steering. Mopar electronic ignition and LED exterior light bulbs were installed under prior ownership, while the front seats were reupholstered, the steering wheel was refurbished, and the brakes were overhauled. The car was then purchased by the seller on BaT in December 2024 and subsequently prepped for The Great Race 2026, a nine-day, 2,300-mile rally celebrating the 100th anniversary of Route 66. This Imperial is now offered at no reserve with a window sticker, 1969 purchase paperwork, broadcast sheets, a brochure, spare parts, receipts, a Great Race medal, and a clean Tennessee title.",
